# Packages blocked from auto-upgrade (require manual migration).
#
# NOTE: do NOT add entries for versions that are merely too fresh. check-deps.ts
# reads the .ci/config/release-age.json window and automatically defers (does not fail on)
# any `latest` published inside that window — npm cannot install it yet anyway,
# and it clears itself once the version ages out. Only blocklist packages held
# back for a real reason (breaking major, native rebuild, pin conflict, etc.).
#
# Format: package-name  # BLOCKER: <substantive reason>
#
# The BLOCKER convention is enforced by scripts/lib/blocker-validator.ts
# (invoked from scripts/gates/check-deps.ts): each line needs a 30+ char reason
# that does not match the banned-phrase list. Blank line = end of group.
#
# To upgrade a blocked package: remove its line from this file and run
#   npm run check:deps -- --upgrade
#
# A LINE HOLDS A MAJOR FOR 90 DAYS, NOT FOREVER (operator ruling 2026-10-01).
# check-deps.ts ages every blocklisted breaking bump from the first stable,
# non-deprecated release of the first line past the current version: it warns
# at 60 days and fails at 90 unless .ci/policy/deps-major-exceptions.json
# excuses it with an owner, a reason and exactly one of a re-checked blocker
# (peer-range, engine-floor) or an expiry at most 30 days out. Minor holds
# are outside the clock.

# ESLint v10 — blocked until typescript-eslint, eslint-plugin-import, eslint-plugin-react support v10
@eslint/js  # BLOCKER: v10.x requires eslint v10; typescript-eslint/import/react plugins lack v10 peer dep support

# @types/node major must match Node engine version (24.x)
@types/node  # BLOCKER: v25+ targets Node 25 APIs; our engines field and CI runners are on Node 24

# eslint-plugin-unicorn v66 — major release with new/renamed lint rules
eslint-plugin-unicorn  # BLOCKER: v66 is a major release that adds and renames lint rules which would surface new violations across the whole monorepo; adoption deferred to a dedicated lint-tooling PR that audits and fixes the rule-set changes

# ESLint v10 core — same constraint as @eslint/js: plugin ecosystem lacks v10 support
eslint  # BLOCKER: v10 requires typescript-eslint/import/react plugin majors that have no eslint v10 peer support yet; take together with @eslint/js in a dedicated lint-tooling PR

# typescript v7 — the lint stack does not accept it yet (console and private/account alike)
typescript  # BLOCKER: typescript-eslint 8.70.1, @typescript-eslint/parser 8.70.1 and @typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin 8.70.1 declare peer typescript ">=4.8.4 <6.1.0" and no release accepts 7 (newest tags 8.70.2-alpha.*); console and account both stay on ^6.0.3 so check:version agrees. Lift when typescript-eslint ships a TS 7 peer range (measured 2026-09-24).
# private/account/web portal build majors (held 2026-09-26; surfaced when check:deps began judging sub-manifest majors)
private/account:stripe  # BLOCKER: stripe 22 -> 23 is a payments API major (published 2026-10-01); the account server's checkout, webhook and subscription code must be migrated against the 23 changelog and proven by the stripe-sandbox CI job in its own change, not taken as a dependency bump
private/account/e2e:stripe  # BLOCKER: the account e2e suite's stripe client moves together with the account server's stripe 23 migration, so both run against one API version
